<!-- ALIVE mark: a flame.

     The viewport hugs the art: this is a mark that stands beside a figure, and
     a square box with the flame floating in the middle of it puts a hand's width
     of nothing between the two. The canvas is 10x12 because that is the shape of
     the flame itself - the base sits on the last row, the tip on the first.

     Three tones, the way fire is actually drawn: an ink contour because it sits
     on the pale-gold streak tile, a red body, and a bright yellow core at the
     base where the heat is. The tip leans right so it reads as fire and not as a
     leaf. -->
